        "title": "Fiber Materials: Natural and Synthetic Rope Fibers",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "All rope starts as a fiber. The fiber determines everything downstream: the achievable strength, elongation behavior, chemical resistance, UV stability, and cost. Natural fibers dominated for 5,000 years; synthetic fibers have been displacing them since DuPont's nylon in 1938. Modern high-performance applications use exclusively synthetic."
